{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"carbonous-bipartisan-ammonite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nWhen `REBAR_ROOT` is unset, every library read rediscovers the code repo root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, through `repo_root` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:53`), which `config.tracker_dir` and `config.load_config` call on each read. Measured on a throwaway two-repo store with the freshness marker fresh, after the synonymous-destined-cricket fix:\n\n- `rebar.show_ticket`: 5 git spawns. 2 come from `_reads._tracker` → `config.tracker_dir` (one direct, one via `load_config`), 2 from the same path in the cross-session warning's own read, and 1 from `cross_session.cross_session_warning_for` → `load_config`.\n- `rebar.list_tickets`: 2 git spawns (`tracker_dir` and `load_config`).\n\nWith `REBAR_ROOT` set, or an explicit `repo_root` (as `rebar audit serve` passes), the same reads spawn 0. The root of a process's cwd does not change between reads in one process, so these are repeated lookups of the same answer.\n\nDiscovered while fixing synonymous-destined-cricket (40c3-d22a-3872-4c8c), whose scope is the freshness throttle only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A library `show_ticket` with `REBAR_ROOT` unset, run from inside a git work tree, starts at most 1 `rev-parse --show-toplevel`, shown by a git-spawn-count test.\n- [ ] A cwd change between reads still resolves the new cwd's repo root, shown by a test.","id":"46ec-e50d-49f6-4774","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Library reads rediscover the repo root with git on every call when REBAR_ROOT is unset"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793818055831750001,"uuid":"b9184801-c886-478a-99a6-9600ae1e1a10"}